        "date": "2026-11-12T16:29:08Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(turning): read the holder side without a thread's antipodal arc ends\n\nThe thread kernel winds each pass in half-turn XY arcs about the axis\nwhose ends alternate onto the antipode, so the raw from/to reading put\nevery threading path on both sides of the spindle and refused it (and\nits drawn body). The holder side is now read from the moves' meridian\npieces with round arcs about the axis left out (a meridian arc's chords\ncount, catching a bulge past its ends), and those round arcs are read\nat |rho| on the holder's side. A near side off the axis while the far\nside reaches under twice PAST_CENTRE is refused instead of guessed.\n\nPinned by a_thread_pass_winding_through_the_antipode_is_judged_not_refused,\nthe_drawn_body_flips_its_radial_with_the_holder_side and the extended\nthe_side_is_where_the_path_reaches_and_a_past_centre_overrun_keeps_it.\n\nRefs #1102\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
